/*
 * Declares the CmpPointerOperatorValue class.
 *
 * CmpPointerOperatorValue represents binary comparison operations where at
 * least one operand is a pointer. Pointer comparisons differ from arithmetic
 * or structural comparisons because they operate on pointer identity and
 * address ordering rather than on the values pointed to.
 *
 * Supported comparisons typically include:
 *   - equality / inequality,
 *   - relational comparisons when allowed by the language semantics,
 *   - null-pointer checks.
 *
 * The result of any pointer comparison is always a boolean value.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::pointer::cmp
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/pointer/cmp.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-03
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
